Make CircularBuffer.append sync-free (mjlab 1.3.0).

`if torch.any(is_first_push)` copies a bool from the GPU every call. The
actuator delay buffers append once per physics substep, so each env step
stalled the CPU on the GPU four times and the Python side of the step could
not overlap physics. The masked torch.where fills the same history without
the readback: ~10% faster env steps at 4096 envs on the RTX 4090 laptop.

--- a/mjlab/utils/buffers/circular_buffer.py
+++ b/mjlab/utils/buffers/circular_buffer.py
@@ -208,9 +208,10 @@
     self._buffer[self._pointer] = data
 
     # Backfill entire history with first frame for newly initialized batches.
-    is_first_push = self._num_pushes == 0
-    if torch.any(is_first_push):
-      self._buffer[:, is_first_push] = data[is_first_push]
+    # torch.where rather than `if torch.any(...)`: the branch would block the
+    # CPU on the GPU every physics substep.
+    is_first_push = (self._num_pushes == 0).view(1, -1, *([1] * (data.dim() - 1)))
+    torch.where(is_first_push, data.unsqueeze(0), self._buffer, out=self._buffer)
 
     self._num_pushes += 1
 
